598
00:28:40.380 --> 00:28:41.500
Steve Nash is so cool.
史蒂夫·纳什太酷了。

599
00:28:43.280 --> 00:28:45.160
I have a location alert.
我有一个外景地提醒。

600
00:28:45.620 --> 00:28:51.980
Both the exterior and interior of Frame Select was a building on Alameda Boulevard in Burbank.
Frame Select的内外景都是在伯班克阿拉米达大道上的一栋建筑里拍摄的。

601
00:28:52.220 --> 00:28:57.580
The office was an empty suite that our set decorating crew, led by Steve Rothstein, had filled up.
这间办公室原本是空的，由史蒂夫·罗斯坦带领的布景团队把它填满了。

602
00:28:57.760 --> 00:29:01.360
That big Frame Select logo, I mean, it's very large.
那个巨大的“Frame Select”标志，我是说，它真的非常大。

603
00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:02.200
It's huge.
简直巨大。

604
00:29:02.400 --> 00:29:03.200
Over reception.
就在接待处上方。

605
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:04.960
I noticed it.
我注意到了。

606
00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:10.400
It was designed by Michael Gallenberg and Henry Sane and then built by our construction crew, headed by Tim James.
它是由迈克尔·加伦伯格和亨利·塞恩设计的，然后由蒂姆·詹姆斯带领的施工团队建造的。

607
00:29:11.100 --> 00:29:13.020
I felt like there was a story there.
我觉得这背后有个故事。

608
00:29:13.200 --> 00:29:17.100
I've never seen us make such a large sign for a company.
我从没见过我们为一家公司制作过这么大的招牌。

609
00:29:17.660 --> 00:29:19.220
What does this tell us?
这说明了什么？

610
00:29:19.860 --> 00:29:22.100
Also, Frame Select is very busy.
而且，Frame Select 看起来非常忙碌。

611
00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:24.580
Did you see all the people coming and going?
你看到那些进进出出的人了吗？

612
00:29:24.740 --> 00:29:25.160
I did.
看到了。

613
00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:26.500
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

614
00:29:26.740 --> 00:29:29.000
They're a big deal with lots of activity.
他们是个大公司，业务非常繁忙。

615
00:29:29.300 --> 00:29:29.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

616
00:29:30.100 --> 00:29:32.060
Well, we have a little bit of Dwight Sass.
好吧，我们来聊聊德怀特的毒舌。

617
00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:38.040
When they go into the lobby, Dwight tells Jim he should check in with the receptionist because he's good with receptionists.
当他们走进大厅时，德怀特告诉吉姆他应该去前台登记，因为他很擅长应付前台接待员。

618
00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:38.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

619
00:29:38.740 --> 00:29:39.640
Dwight Sass.
德怀特的毒舌。

620
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:43.880
But they, um, they run out of Frame Select.
但他们，嗯，他们从 Frame Select 跑了出来。

621
00:29:44.480 --> 00:29:49.060
They duck back out of the lobby because Danny Cordray is sitting there.
他们躲回了大厅外面，因为丹尼·科德雷正坐在那里。

622
00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:52.740
The frickin' Danny Cordray.
该死的丹尼·科德雷。

623
00:29:53.120 --> 00:29:56.860
He is the worst, meaning the best, salesman ever.
他是史上最差劲，也就是最厉害的销售员。

624
00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:01.060
He works at Osprey Paper, and he keeps taking all of their clients.
他在鱼鹰纸业工作，一直在抢走他们的所有客户。

625
00:30:01.440 --> 00:30:02.620
Well, you know what this means.
好吧，你知道这意味着什么。

626
00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:03.680
Oh, I do.
哦，我知道。

627
00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:06.160
It's a guest star alert, and it's a big one.
这是客串明星预警，而且是个大牌。

628
00:30:06.320 --> 00:30:07.040
It is.
确实。

629
00:30:07.600 --> 00:30:11.940
Timothy Oliphant, star of Deadwood, star of Justified.
蒂莫西·奥利芬特，《死木》的主演，《火线警探》的主演。

630
00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:13.780
Also in The Mandalorian.
还出演了《曼达洛人》。

631
00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:14.640
Woo-woo!
呜呼！

632
00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:17.380
Plays Danny Cordray.
他饰演丹尼·科德雷。

633
00:30:17.760 --> 00:30:19.960
We had a fan question from Natalie F.
我们收到了来自德克萨斯州圣安东尼奥市娜塔莉·F的粉丝提问。

634
00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:21.280
in San Antonio, Texas.
请告诉我们关于和蒂莫西·奥利芬特合作的一切，他是怎么来到这个节目的？

635
00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:27.800
Please tell us everything about working with Timothy Oliphant, and how did he come to be on the show?
嗯，我的记忆是明迪·卡灵专门为这个角色推荐了他，他就是这样得到这份工作的。

636
00:30:28.060 --> 00:30:33.540
Well, my memory is that Mindy Kaling specifically pitched him for this role, and that's how he got the job.
这对我来说说得通。

637
00:30:33.680 --> 00:30:35.800
And it makes sense to me.
她写了这一集，后来他也出演了《明迪烦事多》。

638
00:30:35.960 --> 00:30:39.080
She wrote this episode, and then later he had a role in The Mindy Project, too.
所以她是他的粉丝。

639
00:30:39.200 --> 00:30:40.000
So she was a fan.
没错。

640
00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:40.480
Yeah.
是啊。

641
00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:42.240
I loved working with him.
我很喜欢和他一起工作。

642
00:30:42.380 --> 00:30:43.280
He was so fun.
他太有趣了。

643
00:30:43.460 --> 00:30:44.820
He was so fun.
他真的太有趣了。

644
00:30:45.100 --> 00:30:51.180
I also was on Conan O'Brien the same night he was a guest, and he brought some kind of fancy whiskey we all got to drink.
我和他还在同一晚做客过柯南·奥布莱恩的节目，他带了一些高级威士忌，我们都有幸喝到了。

645
00:30:51.260 --> 00:30:52.120
He's a lot of fun.
他是个很有趣的人。

646
00:30:52.560 --> 00:30:53.360
He's great.
他太棒了。

647
00:30:53.600 --> 00:30:53.720
Yeah.
是啊。

648
00:30:53.860 --> 00:30:57.760
Speaking of Conan, have you heard Conan's podcast interview with him?
说到柯南，你听过柯南对他进行的播客采访吗？

649
00:30:57.840 --> 00:30:58.680
It's so good, you guys.
真的太棒了，伙计们。

650
00:30:58.680 --> 00:30:59.740
He is so funny.
他太搞笑了。

651
00:30:59.760 --> 00:31:00.360
They're hilarious.
他们太搞笑了。

652
00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:03.300
When he takes over doing the ads, I was cracking up.
当他接手拍广告时，我简直笑得前仰后合。

653
00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:04.600
That's a good listen, you guys.
那期节目很值得一听，伙计们。

654
00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:06.020
We reached out to him.
我们联系了他。

655
00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:09.840
He's currently filming Justified in Chicago, the reboot of Justified.
他目前正在芝加哥拍摄《火线警探》的重启版。

656
00:31:10.020 --> 00:31:15.680
But I found an old interview with him where he talked about his time on The Office.
但我翻出了一段他的旧采访，他在里面谈到了自己在《办公室》剧组的时光。

657
00:31:16.200 --> 00:31:17.220
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

658
00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:19.740
They had a whole EPK set up over in the warehouse.
他们在仓库里专门搭建了一个电子新闻资料包（EPK）拍摄区。

659
00:31:19.740 --> 00:31:20.800
I remember this.
我记得这个。

660
00:31:20.960 --> 00:31:25.620
Well, here is Timothy Oliphant talking about how he was excited to be on the show.
好了，下面是蒂莫西·奥利芬特谈论他当时能参演该剧有多兴奋。

661
00:31:26.540 --> 00:31:27.860
I wanted to be on it.
我当时就想参演。

662
00:31:28.180 --> 00:31:33.040
So I was just like, it was a, I've been a fan of the show for forever.
所以我当时就觉得，这真是……我一直是这部剧的忠实粉丝。

663
00:31:33.260 --> 00:31:37.240
And so when I got that call, it was fantastic.
所以当我接到那个电话时，感觉太棒了。

664
00:31:37.620 --> 00:31:41.060
You know, they asked that, you know, that they wanted me to be on the show.
你知道，他们问我，你知道，他们想让我参演这部剧。

665
00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:41.640
I said, sure.
我说，没问题。

666
00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:43.400
What do I, what do I play?
我演什么角色？

667
00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:51.060
I play a character named Danny Cordray, and he is, when we meet him, he is a rival salesman
我演一个叫丹尼·科德雷的角色，当我们见到他时，他是一个销售竞争对手，

668
00:31:51.060 --> 00:31:54.220
who has done quite well.
而且业绩相当出色。

669
00:31:54.360 --> 00:32:00.560
He's a bit of a problem for the guys in The Office, the enemy, quote unquote.
他让《办公室》里的那帮人感到有些棘手，算是所谓的“敌人”吧。

670
00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:07.660
And to further kind of complicate things, once dated Pam.
而且更复杂的是，他曾经和帕姆约会过。

671
00:32:09.420 --> 00:32:18.200
And there seems to be, as the story goes, some discrepancy over whether that didn't work
故事里似乎还有些分歧，关于那段感情没成，

672
00:32:18.200 --> 00:32:21.460
out because of her or that didn't work out because of me.
是因为她，还是因为我。

673
00:32:21.620 --> 00:32:26.980
And it's quite the subject of conversation.
这成了大家热议的话题。

674
00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:29.180
I'm not going to lie.
我不撒谎。

675
00:32:30.080 --> 00:32:39.440
I love the implication that perhaps someone of Timothy Oliphant's, what do I say?
我很喜欢这种暗示，就是像蒂莫西·奥利芬特这样的人，该怎么说呢？

676
00:32:40.180 --> 00:32:40.740
Hotness?
性感的人？

677
00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:42.320
Yes, would date me.
没错，会跟我约会。

678
00:32:42.640 --> 00:32:45.620
I was like, I'll take it.
我当时就想，我接受。

679
00:32:45.720 --> 00:32:46.000
Yeah.
是啊。

680
00:32:46.340 --> 00:32:49.180
Even if he wasn't interested in a second or third date.
哪怕他没兴趣进行第二次或第三次约会。

681
00:32:49.740 --> 00:32:52.880
It made for such a funny dynamic between Jim and Pam.
这让吉姆和帕姆之间的互动变得非常有趣。

682
00:32:53.060 --> 00:32:53.920
It was so good.
真的太棒了。

683
00:32:54.100 --> 00:32:56.520
Oh my gosh, costume contest next week.
天哪，下周要举办变装大赛了。

684
00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:57.140
Oh yeah.
噢，没错。

685
00:32:57.340 --> 00:32:59.000
Oh, I mean.
噢，我是说。

686
00:32:59.870 --> 00:33:00.420
I'll wait.
我等着看。

687
00:33:01.320 --> 00:33:03.460
Timothy really fit in right from the beginning.
蒂莫西从一开始就完美融入了剧组。

688
00:33:03.780 --> 00:33:05.920
He was just great to work with.
和他合作真是太棒了。

689
00:33:06.180 --> 00:33:11.620
And this last clip really shows you how he had become part of our family.
最后这段视频真的展示了他如何成为了我们大家庭的一员。

690
00:33:12.280 --> 00:33:17.300
Really, I was just so genuinely flattered that they'd have me and give me an opportunity to
真的，我当时真心感到受宠若惊，他们能邀请我，给我机会，

691
00:33:17.300 --> 00:33:21.200
do something that's really so different than just about anything I've done.
让我做一些和我之前做过的任何事都截然不同的尝试。

692
00:33:21.340 --> 00:33:24.820
And I just, I really feel quite blessed.
我真的觉得自己很幸运。

693
00:33:24.820 --> 00:33:26.180
And it's just been a kick.
这真的太有趣了。

694
00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:31.640
So, rain kind of bugs me.
所以，雷恩有点让我心烦。

695
00:33:33.040 --> 00:33:35.120
But, you know, everyone else, fantastic.
但是，你知道，其他人，都很棒。

696
00:33:35.460 --> 00:33:36.280
You know, it's been great.
你知道，这感觉很棒。

697
00:33:37.640 --> 00:33:40.120
I mean, he got it that we dog on rain.
我是说，他明白我们是在开雷恩的玩笑。

698
00:33:40.240 --> 00:33:40.420
Yeah.
没错。

699
00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:41.060
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吗？

700
00:33:41.120 --> 00:33:44.300
That's when you know you're in, is when you can take a shot at rain.
当你能拿雷恩开涮时，你就知道你已经真正融入我们了。

701
00:33:44.780 --> 00:33:45.840
That is very funny.
那太搞笑了。

702
00:33:45.840 --> 00:33:48.820
And also, I wasn't expecting it because he was being so sincere.
而且我完全没料到，因为他当时表现得那么真诚。

703
00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:49.360
I know.
我知道。

704
00:33:49.560 --> 00:33:50.620
That's why he's so great.
这就是他为什么那么棒的原因。

705
00:33:50.920 --> 00:33:56.500
We got a fan mail flurry, also Angela, about Danny Cordray's name.
安吉拉，我们还收到了一大波关于丹尼·科德雷这个名字的粉丝来信。

706
00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:59.940
People wanted to know if it was inspired by Randy Cordray.
大家想知道这名字是不是受兰迪·科德雷的启发。

707
00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:01.500
It was.
确实是。

708
00:34:02.020 --> 00:34:02.500
Absolutely.
没错。

709
00:34:03.100 --> 00:34:05.360
We actually reached out to Randy about this.
我们其实就这件事联系了兰迪。

710
00:34:05.440 --> 00:34:09.580
And he said, you might remember that my office was next door to Mindy Kaling.
他说，你们可能还记得我的办公室就在敏迪·卡灵隔壁。

711
00:34:09.860 --> 00:34:15.640
One day in the weeks prior to the script coming out, Mindy came by and said, Randy, you have
剧本出来前几周的一天，敏迪走过来对我说，兰迪，你的

712
00:34:15.640 --> 00:34:16.520
a cool last name.
姓氏很酷。

713
00:34:16.740 --> 00:34:18.620
Can I use it for a character I'm writing?
我能把它用在我正在写的一个角色身上吗？

714
00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:19.960
And I said, sure.
我说，当然可以。

715
00:34:20.160 --> 00:34:22.280
And that's how Danny Cordray got his name.
丹尼·科德雷的名字就是这么来的。

716
00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:27.160
Randy said he was really flattered to have someone as cool as Timothy Oliphant having his
兰迪说，能让像蒂莫西·奥利芬特这么酷的人在剧里用

717
00:34:27.160 --> 00:34:28.520
own last name on the show.
自己的姓氏，他感到非常荣幸。

718
00:34:28.520 --> 00:34:32.320
And he says, people still come up to him and say, you know, there's a character in
他说，现在还有人会跑过来跟他说，你知道吗，在《办公室》里

719
00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:33.700
the office that has your last name.
有个角色用了你的姓氏。

720
00:34:35.420 --> 00:34:36.900
Oh, that's amazing.
噢，那太棒了。

721
00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:40.240
Back at the office, Andy is starting to spiral.
回到办公室，安迪开始失控了。

722
00:34:40.480 --> 00:34:41.400
We mentioned this earlier.
我们之前提到过这一点。

723
00:34:41.400 --> 00:34:47.040
He's gotten his Cornell alumni magazine and has learned that Broccoli Rob has this milk
他收到了康奈尔大学的校友杂志，发现西兰花罗布拍了个牛奶

724
00:34:47.040 --> 00:34:48.940
commercial that he's singing in.
广告，还在里面唱歌。

725
00:34:49.280 --> 00:34:51.260
And Andy can't take it.
安迪受不了了。

726
00:34:51.480 --> 00:34:53.020
Andy was the musical one.
安迪才是那个搞音乐的。

727
00:34:53.180 --> 00:34:55.100
He had more solos than Broccoli Rob.
他的独唱机会比西兰花罗布多。

728
00:34:55.300 --> 00:34:56.900
And now Broccoli Rob has a commercial.
可现在西兰花罗布竟然拍了广告。

729
00:34:57.500 --> 00:35:03.660
Listen, not only that, he's collaborating with Trey Anastasio, the guitarist from Phish.
听着，不仅如此，他还和Phish乐队的吉他手特雷·阿纳斯塔西奥合作了。

730
00:35:03.820 --> 00:35:04.340
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

731
00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:08.760
And there's a quote about how great that collaboration was.
而且还有一段引语夸赞这次合作有多棒。

732
00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:10.820
I mean, he doesn't know what to do with himself.
我是说，他都不知道该怎么办才好了。

733
00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:13.260
We had a fan question from Anne S.
我们收到了一位来自瑞士苏黎世的粉丝安妮·S的提问。

734
00:35:13.420 --> 00:35:14.580
in Zurich, Switzerland.
你好，苏黎世的安妮。

735
00:35:15.160 --> 00:35:16.800
Hello, Anne from Zurich.
这个问题跨越了很远的距离。

736
00:35:16.800 --> 00:35:18.740
This question traveled a long way.
这个问题跨越了很远的距离。

737
00:35:19.020 --> 00:35:24.300
When Andy is reading the Cornell alumni magazine, Cornell is written in purple.
当安迪读康奈尔校友杂志时，上面的“康奈尔”字样是紫色的。

738
00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:28.820
It seems very odd for a school magazine to not be in the school colors.
校刊不用学校代表色，这看起来很奇怪。

739
00:35:29.120 --> 00:35:31.540
Did you have to do this for copyright reasons?
是因为版权原因才这么做的吗？

740
00:35:31.760 --> 00:35:34.220
Ah, what a smart catch.
啊，真是个敏锐的发现。

741
00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:35.960
I asked Randy.
我问了兰迪。

742
00:35:36.240 --> 00:35:40.920
He said that was a real Cornell alumni magazine that Phil Shea got a real one.
他说那是菲尔·谢找来的真正的康奈尔校友杂志。

743
00:35:41.420 --> 00:35:44.580
And I looked it up, and sometimes they print the name in purple.
我查了一下，他们有时确实会用紫色印刷校名。

744
00:35:45.100 --> 00:35:46.000
Don't know why.
不知道为什么。

745
00:35:46.160 --> 00:35:46.740
Don't know why.
不知道为什么。

746
00:35:46.860 --> 00:35:47.620
But it was real.
但那是真的。

747
00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:49.160
It's a Cornell mystery.
这是个康奈尔之谜。

