He went on his computer.
他打开了电脑。

1057
00:50:15.510 --> 00:50:16.530
He pulled it up.
他调出了页面。

1058
00:50:16.830 --> 00:50:19.470
There's a photo of Danny with the backpack.
上面有丹尼背着那个背包的照片。

1059
00:50:19.990 --> 00:50:21.530
It's so great.
太棒了。

1060
00:50:21.750 --> 00:50:23.010
It's in deleted scenes.
这在删减片段里。

1061
00:50:23.170 --> 00:50:24.010
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1062
00:50:24.310 --> 00:50:28.590
Randy shared with us that Michael Gallenberg shot this photo on green screen.
兰迪告诉我们，这张照片是迈克尔·加伦伯格在绿幕前拍的。

1063
00:50:28.590 --> 00:50:33.490
Henry Sane photoshopped the image into purchase stock backgrounds from Getty Images.
亨利·塞恩用Photoshop把照片合成到了从盖蒂图片社购买的背景图上。

1064
00:50:33.910 --> 00:50:36.710
Henry also built the fakie webpage for it.
亨利还为此做了一个假网页。

1065
00:50:36.970 --> 00:50:41.970
And Randy gave us the full resolution image of the backpack photo shoot.
兰迪还给了我们背包拍摄的高清原图。

1066
00:50:42.250 --> 00:50:43.330
They are amazing.
它们太惊人了。

1067
00:50:43.930 --> 00:50:45.870
I'm going to put them in Office Ladies Pod Stories.
我会把它们放到《办公室女士》的播客故事里。

1068
00:50:46.110 --> 00:50:53.510
But imagine with me, Timothy Oliphant as Danny, giving a very moody, kind of sassy glance over
但请跟我一起想象一下，蒂莫西·奥利芬特饰演的丹尼，背着背包，

1069
00:50:53.510 --> 00:50:55.710
his shoulder as he has a backpack on.
回过头来，眼神忧郁又带着一丝俏皮。

1070
00:50:58.320 --> 00:50:59.720
The photos are amazing.
这些照片太棒了。

1071
00:50:59.980 --> 00:51:03.880
I feel like Danny Cordray is everything Michael wishes he could be.
我觉得丹尼·科德雷就是迈克尔梦想成为的一切。

1072
00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:04.680
I mean.
我是说。

1073
00:51:04.820 --> 00:51:05.620
Male model.
男模特。

1074
00:51:06.320 --> 00:51:07.600
Jansport male model.
Jansport的男模特。

1075
00:51:08.100 --> 00:51:08.300
Yeah.
没错。

1076
00:51:08.540 --> 00:51:08.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1077
00:51:08.800 --> 00:51:10.120
Top salesperson.
顶级销售员。

1078
00:51:10.380 --> 00:51:10.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1079
00:51:11.120 --> 00:51:17.540
Well, when Michael and Jim and Dwight go in to meet with Steve Nash, they really pitch him hard.
好吧，当迈克尔、吉姆和德怀特去见史蒂夫·纳什时，他们真的极力推销。

1080
00:51:17.680 --> 00:51:20.620
They say, we will deliver on the weekends.
他们说，我们周末也能送货。

1081
00:51:20.920 --> 00:51:23.180
We'll give you all of our paper at coSt.
我们所有的纸张都按成本价给你。

1082
00:51:23.220 --> 00:51:24.380
He's like, shake my hand.
他说，跟我握手。

1083
00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:25.380
Shake my hand now.
现在就跟我握手。

1084
00:51:25.680 --> 00:51:30.200
And even still, Steve Nash is going to go with Danny Cordray.
即便如此，史蒂夫·纳什还是选择了丹尼·科德雷。

1085
00:51:30.760 --> 00:51:31.980
Michael can't believe it.
迈克尔简直不敢相信。

1086
00:51:32.420 --> 00:51:33.220
Guest star alert.
客串明星预警。

1087
00:51:33.440 --> 00:51:35.580
Steve Nash was played by Pete Pastor.
史蒂夫·纳什由皮特·帕斯托饰演。

1088
00:51:36.020 --> 00:51:39.140
He has appeared on Seinfeld, Chicago Hope, and Passions.
他曾出演过《宋飞正传》、《芝加哥希望》和《激情》。

1089
00:51:39.980 --> 00:51:41.680
Not interested in Michael's deal.
对迈克尔的交易不感兴趣。

1090
00:51:42.380 --> 00:51:42.700
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1091
00:51:43.100 --> 00:51:44.860
Well, the guys are really frustrated now.
好吧，这几个人现在真的很沮丧。

1092
00:51:44.980 --> 00:51:46.400
They're going to leave Frame Select.
他们准备离开Frame Select公司。

1093
00:51:46.760 --> 00:51:47.940
Dwight blames Jim.
德怀特怪罪吉姆。

1094
00:51:48.300 --> 00:51:50.300
Michael says they just simply got bested.
迈克尔说他们只是单纯地技不如人。

1095
00:51:50.420 --> 00:51:53.340
They're going to get in the elevators, kind of dejected, and go home.
他们垂头丧气地走进电梯，准备回家。

1096
00:51:53.340 --> 00:52:00.940
We had a fan question from Anu Yu in Estonia and Karis D from West Wales, UK, and others.
我们收到了来自爱沙尼亚的Anu Yu、英国西威尔士的Karis D以及其他人的粉丝提问。

1097
00:52:01.240 --> 00:52:06.960
Was it scripted or improv at 7 minutes and 45 seconds when Michael says,
在7分45秒时，迈克尔说，

1098
00:52:06.960 --> 00:52:11.000
why is there a door close button if it doesn't even close the door?
如果关门键根本关不上门，那它存在的意义是什么？这段是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的？

1099
00:52:11.420 --> 00:52:12.560
That was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

1100
00:52:12.860 --> 00:52:15.580
And I did a deep dive on door close buttons.
我还专门深入研究了一下电梯的关门键。

1101
00:52:16.100 --> 00:52:16.620
What?
什么？

1102
00:52:17.460 --> 00:52:20.720
Have you ever wondered about the door close button?
你有没有想过电梯里的“关门”按钮？

1103
00:52:21.520 --> 00:52:24.200
Like, does it really close the door on elevators?
比如，它真的能关上电梯门吗？

1104
00:52:24.420 --> 00:52:25.320
Does it really work?
它真的有用吗？

1105
00:52:25.320 --> 00:52:28.180
I have never wondered about this.
我从来没想过这个问题。

1106
00:52:28.380 --> 00:52:33.340
Well, I had this faint memory of this story coming out years ago that said,
好吧，我隐约记得几年前有篇报道说，

1107
00:52:33.620 --> 00:52:34.980
door close buttons don't work.
关门按钮根本没用。

1108
00:52:35.440 --> 00:52:35.980
Oh.
哦。

1109
00:52:36.400 --> 00:52:37.760
So I looked into it.
所以我去查了一下。

1110
00:52:37.920 --> 00:52:39.560
Do the door open buttons work?
那开门按钮有用吗？

1111
00:52:39.720 --> 00:52:41.120
Door open buttons work.
开门按钮是有用的。

1112
00:52:41.380 --> 00:52:46.160
Door close ones are just to fake us out so we feel like we're getting somewhere because we're in a hurry.
关门按钮只是为了糊弄我们，让我们觉得因为赶时间而有所作为。

1113
00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:47.800
That's exactly right, Angela.
你说得太对了，安吉拉。

1114
00:52:47.800 --> 00:52:48.500
Come on.
得了吧。

1115
00:52:48.860 --> 00:52:51.660
The New York Times did a piece on door close buttons.
《纽约时报》曾专门报道过关门按钮。

1116
00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:54.240
Here's the scoop.
真相就在这儿。

1117
00:52:54.480 --> 00:52:56.360
This is a mom detective moment.
这可是“妈妈侦探”的高光时刻。

1118
00:52:56.560 --> 00:52:57.960
I'm so proud of myself.
我真为自己感到骄傲。

1119
00:52:58.580 --> 00:53:00.100
All I did was look up an article.
我不过是查了篇文章而已。

1120
00:53:00.240 --> 00:53:01.620
I mean, someone else figured it out.
我是说，那是别人研究出来的。

1121
00:53:02.360 --> 00:53:05.020
Most elevator door buttons do not work.
大多数电梯的关门按钮都不起作用。

1122
00:53:05.380 --> 00:53:09.620
In 1990, we passed the Americans with Disabilities Act.
1990年，我们通过了《美国残疾人法案》。

1123
00:53:10.060 --> 00:53:10.520
Okay.
好的。

1124
00:53:11.060 --> 00:53:17.400
Part of that legislation required that elevator doors remain open long enough for anyone who might be using
该法案的一部分要求电梯门必须保持开启足够长的时间，以便让使用

1125
00:53:17.400 --> 00:53:21.080
crutches, a cane, or a wheelchair to enter and exit.
拐杖、手杖或轮椅的人能够进出。

1126
00:53:21.300 --> 00:53:25.120
And as a result, door close buttons were phased out.
结果，关门按钮就被逐步淘汰了。

1127
00:53:25.640 --> 00:53:26.920
They used to work.
它们以前是管用的。

1128
00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:31.160
But after this legislation was passed, they did away with them.
但这项法案通过后，它们就被取消了。

1129
00:53:31.480 --> 00:53:32.860
But they left the button?
但他们留下了按钮？

1130
00:53:33.080 --> 00:53:33.660
Yes.
是的。

1131
00:53:34.100 --> 00:53:40.420
Because that way they could be operated by firefighters or maintenance workers in the case of an emergency,
因为这样的话，消防员或维修人员在紧急情况下可以使用，

1132
00:53:40.720 --> 00:53:43.880
but they only work if you have a proper key or a code.
但它们只有在你有专用钥匙或密码时才起作用。

1133
00:53:44.740 --> 00:53:45.320
Huh.
哈。

1134
00:53:45.600 --> 00:53:46.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:53:46.060 --> 00:53:46.110
Yeah.
没错。

1136
00:53:46.620 --> 00:53:52.060
So none of the door close buttons work in any elevators unless you have a proper key or a code.
所以，除非你有专用钥匙或密码，否则任何电梯里的关门按钮都不起作用。

1137
00:53:52.440 --> 00:53:52.920
That's right.
没错。

1138
00:53:52.940 --> 00:53:53.960
Am I understanding this correctly?
我理解得对吗？

1139
00:53:54.100 --> 00:53:54.360
Yes.
是的。

1140
00:53:54.540 --> 00:53:56.840
So I can tell my kids to quit hitting it over and over?
那我能告诉我的孩子们别再一直按那个按钮了吗？

1141
00:53:57.020 --> 00:53:57.560
That's right.
没错。

1142
00:53:57.860 --> 00:53:58.200
Okay.
好吧。

1143
00:53:58.540 --> 00:53:59.520
But that's not all.
但这还不是全部。

1144
00:53:59.780 --> 00:54:00.060
Okay.
好的。

1145
00:54:00.420 --> 00:54:03.100
The article also covered crosswalk signals.
那篇文章还提到了人行横道的信号灯。

1146
00:54:03.820 --> 00:54:06.540
You know, the button that you press to cross the street?
你知道，就是你过马路时按的那个按钮？

1147
00:54:06.620 --> 00:54:08.200
Yeah, you're kind of obsessed with them.
是啊，你对那些按钮简直有点着迷。

1148
00:54:08.360 --> 00:54:10.340
We were on a walk the other day, and you were like, hmm.
前几天我们散步时，你还说，嗯……

1149
00:54:10.720 --> 00:54:12.360
You were like suspect of one of them.
你当时好像怀疑其中一个按钮。

1150
00:54:12.880 --> 00:54:14.720
Well, it had a sign that said, don't press.
因为它上面写着“请勿按压”。

1151
00:54:14.720 --> 00:54:15.240
I know.
我知道。

1152
00:54:15.340 --> 00:54:16.340
I was like, what's this about?
我当时就在想，这是怎么回事？

1153
00:54:16.520 --> 00:54:16.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1154
00:54:17.400 --> 00:54:22.560
In 2004, New York City deactivated most of the pedestrian buttons.
2004年，纽约市停用了大部分行人过街按钮。

1155
00:54:22.560 --> 00:54:30.500
So of the over 3,000 walk buttons in New York City, more than 2,500 of them were replaced
所以，在纽约市三千多个过街按钮中，有超过2500个被替换成了

1156
00:54:30.500 --> 00:54:31.500
with placebos.
安慰剂按钮。

1157
00:54:31.760 --> 00:54:34.400
They're just there to give the illusion of control.
它们只是为了给人一种掌控感。

1158
00:54:35.220 --> 00:54:40.840
Today, there are only 120 working walk systems controlled by the pedestrian in New York City.
如今，纽约市仅剩下120个由行人控制的过街信号系统。

1159
00:54:40.840 --> 00:54:42.460
Why not just get rid of them?
为什么不干脆拆掉它们呢？

1160
00:54:42.860 --> 00:54:44.360
I don't need your fake button.
我不需要你那假按钮。

1161
00:54:44.580 --> 00:54:45.380
Just get rid of it.
直接拆掉就行了。

1162
00:54:45.880 --> 00:54:46.680
I don't know.
我也不知道。

1163
00:54:46.760 --> 00:54:53.020
But in 2010, ABC News did a study of pedestrian crosswalks in Austin, Texas, Gainesville, Florida,
但在2010年，美国广播公司新闻部对德克萨斯州奥斯汀、佛罗里达州盖恩斯维尔

1164
00:54:53.200 --> 00:54:57.460
and Syracuse, and only one of the signals was actually pedestrian controlled.
以及雪城的人行横道进行了一项研究，结果发现其中只有一个信号灯是真正由行人控制的。

1165
00:54:58.220 --> 00:54:59.900
So, I mean, it's not just New York City.
所以，我的意思是，这不仅仅是纽约市的问题。

1166
00:55:00.280 --> 00:55:00.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1167
00:55:00.480 --> 00:55:05.620
But then I found an article that was written by an engineer who said that pushing the crosswalk
但我后来找到一篇文章，是一位工程师写的，他说按下过街

1168
00:55:05.620 --> 00:55:09.200
button does have an effect, but it's not the effect you might think.
按钮确实有作用，但并不是你以为的那种作用。

1169
00:55:09.460 --> 00:55:17.780
He said most crosswalks are computer controlled, and it's all about traffic, you know, traffic
他说大多数人行横道都是由电脑控制的，一切都是为了交通，你知道的，交通

1170
00:55:17.780 --> 00:55:18.780
maintenance and control.
维护和管制。

1171
00:55:18.780 --> 00:55:24.980
And he said pressing the crosswalk button will not make the light change faster, but what
他说按下过街按钮并不会让红绿灯变快，但它

1172
00:55:24.980 --> 00:55:29.200
it will do is extend the amount of time that you can cross the street.
能延长你过马路的时间。

1173
00:55:29.360 --> 00:55:34.300
So, when it's automatic, there's a certain amount of time allotted for that crosswalk,
所以，当它是自动运行时，过街时间是固定的，

1174
00:55:34.380 --> 00:55:38.600
but if the button is activated, it will stay on longer.
但如果按下了按钮，绿灯时间就会变长。

1175
00:55:38.740 --> 00:55:40.620
So, you can get across the street without running.
这样你过马路时就不用跑了。

1176
00:55:41.140 --> 00:55:41.660
Exactly.
没错。

1177
00:55:41.820 --> 00:55:47.460
What about that intersection by my house where the light rarely turns, and so I pull forward
那我家附近那个路口呢？那里的灯很少变绿，所以我总是往前开

1178
00:55:47.460 --> 00:55:49.980
and pull back and pull forward and pull back over the crosswalk?
再倒车，再往前开再倒车，反复压过人行横道？

1179
00:55:50.100 --> 00:55:50.920
Does that do anything?
那样做有用吗？

1180
00:55:51.600 --> 00:55:52.280
Yeah, right?
是啊，对吧？

1181
00:55:52.440 --> 00:55:57.240
There's that rumor that there's some sort of, I mean, when you say it out loud, it sounds
有个传言说，怎么说呢，当你大声说出来时，听起来

1182
00:55:57.240 --> 00:55:57.920
ridiculous, right?
很荒谬，对吧？

1183
00:55:57.920 --> 00:56:04.200
That there's some sort of like pressure sensor underneath the ground that makes lights change.
说是地下有某种压力传感器能让红绿灯变色。

1184
00:56:04.760 --> 00:56:07.020
I mean, what do you think just when we say it?
我的意思是，我们说出来的时候，你觉得呢？

1185
00:56:07.300 --> 00:56:10.460
Based on all we know now about the buttons, do we think that's real?
基于我们现在对这些按钮的了解，你觉得那是真的吗？

1186
00:56:10.600 --> 00:56:12.760
When you say it out loud, it sounds like it doesn't work.
当你大声说出来时，听起来就像是没用的。

1187
00:56:12.760 --> 00:56:18.080
Like, I mean, what I've done before when I've gotten to one of those places where it like
比如，我以前遇到那种灯

1188
00:56:18.080 --> 00:56:19.760
never changes because...
永远不变绿的情况时，因为……

1189
00:56:19.760 --> 00:56:22.800
Yeah, and by the way, this is an intersection that has like no one there.
是啊，顺便说一下，那个路口根本就没车。

1190
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:24.820
I know, that's why it doesn't change.
我知道，所以它才不变绿。

1191
00:56:25.780 --> 00:56:29.580
What I've done before is I've gotten out of the car and pressed the crosswalk button.
我以前的做法是下车去按那个过街按钮。

1192
00:56:29.700 --> 00:56:30.200
I've done that too.
我也干过。

1193
00:56:30.200 --> 00:56:32.340
And now I realize that I'm doing nothing.
现在我意识到我做的一切都是徒劳。

1194
00:56:32.660 --> 00:56:34.200
I know, I've done that too.
我知道，我也干过。

1195
00:56:35.080 --> 00:56:36.080
Well, there you go.
好吧，这就是答案了。

1196
00:56:36.340 --> 00:56:37.960
Well, that was fascinating.
嗯，这太有意思了。

1197
00:56:37.960 --> 00:56:38.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1198
00:56:38.940 --> 00:56:42.680
The article went on to say that we need these fake buttons.
文章接着说，我们需要这些假按钮。

1199
00:56:43.040 --> 00:56:43.540
Why?
为什么？

1200
00:56:43.720 --> 00:56:45.280
We need the illusion of control.
我们需要那种掌控感。

1201
00:56:45.620 --> 00:56:46.680
It's good for us.
这对我们有好处。

1202
00:56:47.320 --> 00:56:49.940
Oh my gosh, what is this, an episode of Westworld?
天哪，这是什么，西部世界的一集吗？

1203
00:56:50.300 --> 00:56:54.880
Listen, the article had a third category, and I didn't know if I should bring it up, but it's
听着，那篇文章里还有第三个类别，我不知道该不该提，但它是

1204
00:56:54.880 --> 00:56:56.440
about office thermostats.
关于办公室恒温器的。

1205
00:56:56.740 --> 00:56:57.820
None of them work.
它们根本没用。

1206
00:56:57.940 --> 00:56:59.880
They're controlled by some master thing.
它们是由某个主控装置控制的。

1207
00:57:00.580 --> 00:57:08.440
Most buildings, master thermostats, are controlled by a master grid, somewhere not accessible.
大多数建筑的主恒温器都是由一个无法触及的主电网控制的。

1208
00:57:08.740 --> 00:57:14.540
And then the office you rent, they'll put like a fakie box in your office.
