嗯，我想指出两点。

1504
01:10:57.280 --> 01:11:05.240
The first is, from 17 minutes and 37 seconds until 18 minutes and 15 seconds, you can see Danny
第一点是，从17分37秒到18分15秒，你可以看到丹尼·科德雷

1505
01:11:05.240 --> 01:11:10.440
Cordray standing outside of Michael's office in the background of this scene.
站在迈克尔办公室外，就在这一幕的背景里。

1506
01:11:11.060 --> 01:11:13.660
Timothy Oliphant had to stand there the whole entire scene.
蒂莫西·奥利芬特不得不站在那儿拍完了整场戏。

1507
01:11:14.280 --> 01:11:15.660
That's what you need to know.
这就是你们需要知道的。

1508
01:11:15.860 --> 01:11:17.380
He was just standing there.
他当时就站在那儿。

1509
01:11:18.020 --> 01:11:24.280
Also, for my background catch, folks, did anyone else notice that there are no toys?
另外，关于背景细节，伙计们，还有人注意到没有玩具了吗？

1510
01:11:24.560 --> 01:11:25.600
Not a single one.
一个都没有。

1511
01:11:25.760 --> 01:11:27.340
No toys on Michael's desk.
迈克尔的桌上没有玩具。

1512
01:11:27.600 --> 01:11:29.560
Did anyone notice, Angela?
安吉拉，你注意到了吗？

1513
01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:32.500
We got a fan mail flurry about it.
我们收到了很多关于此事的粉丝来信。

1514
01:11:32.600 --> 01:11:33.020
Yes.
是的。

1515
01:11:33.020 --> 01:11:34.000
Brooke J.
来自蒙大拿州的布鲁克·J，

1516
01:11:34.320 --> 01:11:35.880
from Montana, Maggie E.
来自田纳西州的玛吉·E，

1517
01:11:35.980 --> 01:11:37.880
from Tennessee, and many others said,
还有许多其他人问道：

1518
01:11:38.120 --> 01:11:43.340
Why is Michael's office more empty than usual and there aren't any toys on his desk?
为什么迈克尔的办公室比平时更空，而且他桌上没有任何玩具？

1519
01:11:43.500 --> 01:11:44.240
Not a one.
一个都没有。

1520
01:11:44.880 --> 01:11:46.600
Also, Christian H.
还有来自密苏里州独立城的克里斯蒂安·H。

1521
01:11:46.820 --> 01:11:47.860
from Independence, Missouri.
他说：

1522
01:11:48.440 --> 01:11:52.400
It seemed like the bookshelves were missing from Michael's office toward the end of the
在这一集快结束时，迈克尔办公室里的书架好像不见了。

1523
01:11:52.400 --> 01:11:52.800
episode.
它们去哪儿了？

1524
01:11:52.800 --> 01:11:53.900
What happened to them?
发生了什么事？

1525
01:11:54.020 --> 01:11:56.320
Is there a deleted scene or something we don't know about?
是有什么我们不知道的删减片段吗？

1526
01:11:56.640 --> 01:11:57.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1527
01:11:57.220 --> 01:11:58.000
What happened?
到底发生了什么？

1528
01:11:58.000 --> 01:12:02.500
Was this that time there was that funky smell in Michael's office in the carpet and they
是不是那次迈克尔办公室的地毯里有股怪味，

1529
01:12:02.500 --> 01:12:03.120
had to pull it up?
所以他们不得不把它拆了？

1530
01:12:03.120 --> 01:12:04.160
I have a memory of this.
我有这段记忆。

1531
01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:06.280
You mean like in real life or fictionally?
你是说现实生活中还是剧情里？

1532
01:12:06.480 --> 01:12:07.440
In real life.
现实生活中。

1533
01:12:07.740 --> 01:12:09.280
No, I never remember that.
不，我完全不记得有这回事。

1534
01:12:09.580 --> 01:12:14.080
There was a funky smell and they had to disassemble the Michael Scott office?
当时有股怪味，他们不得不拆掉迈克尔·斯科特的办公室？

1535
01:12:14.260 --> 01:12:15.440
I have a memory of that.
我有这段记忆。

1536
01:12:15.440 --> 01:12:16.460
We should ask Randy.
我们应该问问兰迪。

1537
01:12:16.740 --> 01:12:19.380
I just remember one time it got a little stinky.
我只记得有一次确实有点臭。

1538
01:12:20.460 --> 01:12:25.300
Okay, I don't remember that, but I mean, I'm just assuming that they used all of Michael's
好吧，我不记得了，但我猜他们是把迈克尔的所有东西

1539
01:12:25.300 --> 01:12:30.620
stuff to create the Meredith Van Helsing office, and that's where all his furniture went.
都拿去布置梅雷迪思·范海辛的办公室了，他的家具都去那儿了。

1540
01:12:30.960 --> 01:12:31.680
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1541
01:12:31.680 --> 01:12:34.940
They did not use any of his toys in Meredith Van Helsing's office.
他们根本没把他的玩具用在梅雷迪思·范海辛的办公室里。

1542
01:12:35.140 --> 01:12:36.020
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.
哦，哦，哦，哦，哦，哦。

1543
01:12:36.080 --> 01:12:37.400
They used his mug?
他们用了他的马克杯？

1544
01:12:38.200 --> 01:12:42.980
Well, the mug, and he points it out to which Jim says, you know, this isn't a real TV show.
嗯，马克杯用了，而且他指出来的时候，吉姆说，你知道，这不是一部真正的电视剧。

1545
01:12:43.260 --> 01:12:45.160
But were his clackety teeth there?
那他的咔哒响牙齿玩具在吗？

1546
01:12:45.320 --> 01:12:47.420
Was his little squishy ball that goes in and out?
那个能捏来捏去的小软球在吗？

1547
01:12:47.600 --> 01:12:48.180
I don't know.
我不知道。

1548
01:12:48.240 --> 01:12:49.120
Were the little clacky balls there?
那些咔哒响的小球在吗？

1549
01:12:49.380 --> 01:12:50.160
I don't know.
我不知道。

1550
01:12:50.340 --> 01:12:51.680
Maybe the clacky balls were there.
也许那些咔哒响的小球在吧。

1551
01:12:51.760 --> 01:12:52.720
We didn't look close enough.
我们当时没仔细看。

1552
01:12:52.720 --> 01:12:53.660
There were no clacky balls.
根本没有那种撞击球。

1553
01:12:53.740 --> 01:12:54.360
Who wants those?
谁会想要那种东西？

1554
01:12:54.840 --> 01:12:56.600
Why do you need them?
你为什么需要它们？

1555
01:12:56.800 --> 01:12:58.380
Sam got us them and we let them.
山姆给我们买了，我们就收下了。

1556
01:12:58.380 --> 01:12:58.680
Why are you watching them?
你为什么盯着它们看？

1557
01:12:59.100 --> 01:13:03.680
What does it bring your desk to have balls clacking back and forth?
在桌上放几个来回撞击的球有什么意义？

1558
01:13:04.340 --> 01:13:05.200
What is it?
那到底是什么？

1559
01:13:05.280 --> 01:13:06.220
Who invented it?
是谁发明的？

1560
01:13:06.400 --> 01:13:06.680
Well.
这个嘛。

1561
01:13:06.820 --> 01:13:08.500
I never got to the bottom of it.
我一直没搞明白。

1562
01:13:08.620 --> 01:13:09.720
I still don't get it.
我还是不懂。

1563
01:13:09.900 --> 01:13:10.900
Are they relaxing?
它们能让人放松吗？

1564
01:13:11.340 --> 01:13:12.180
What is it?
那是什么？

1565
01:13:12.300 --> 01:13:13.700
I like the clacky balls.
我喜欢那些撞击球。

1566
01:13:14.100 --> 01:13:16.320
Sam got us each a little pair of clacky balls.
山姆给我们每人买了一对小撞击球。

1567
01:13:17.120 --> 01:13:19.500
Sam, I've been wanting to tell you this for some time.
山姆，这件事我想跟你说很久了。

1568
01:13:19.960 --> 01:13:34.440
They were sitting on a low shelf in my home office and we had a friend whose toddler came over and in maybe five seconds put all the clacky balls in one giant knot that no one has been able to undo.
它们当时放在我家书房的低矮架子上，有个朋友带蹒跚学步的孩子来家里，不到五秒钟，就把所有撞击球缠成了一个巨大的死结，到现在都没人能解开。

1569
01:13:34.440 --> 01:13:37.240
We now give it as a challenge to people who come over.
我们现在把它当成给客人的挑战。

1570
01:13:37.420 --> 01:13:40.740
Like, can you undo what a toddler did in five seconds?
比如，你能解开一个幼儿在五秒钟内搞出来的东西吗？

1571
01:13:40.900 --> 01:13:41.940
No one's been able to do it.
没人能做到。

1572
01:13:42.020 --> 01:13:43.720
That makes me actually very happy.
这其实让我挺开心的。

1573
01:13:43.860 --> 01:13:44.940
I'm going to take a picture of it.
我要拍张照。

1574
01:13:44.940 --> 01:13:45.200
Please do.
请务必拍下来。

1575
01:13:46.840 --> 01:13:52.260
I understand that it's like some sort of physics phenomenon, the clacky balls.
我明白那是一种物理现象，那些撞击球。

1576
01:13:52.520 --> 01:13:52.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1577
01:13:52.720 --> 01:13:57.660
But I just don't understand how they became such a popular desk item.
但我就是不明白它们是怎么变成那么受欢迎的办公桌摆件的。

1578
01:13:58.500 --> 01:13:59.580
I just don't get it.
我就是搞不懂。

1579
01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:00.700
I'm going to deep dive it.
我要深入研究一下。

1580
01:14:00.880 --> 01:14:06.420
Maybe it's a special episode of Office Ladies, bonus episode, clacky balls.
也许可以做一期《办公室女士》的特别节目，番外篇，撞击球。

1581
01:14:06.700 --> 01:14:07.820
Where did they come from?
它们是从哪儿来的？

1582
01:14:07.960 --> 01:14:09.480
How did they rise in popularity?
它们是怎么流行起来的？

1583
01:14:10.200 --> 01:14:12.780
Well, I will tune in for your clacky balls episode.
好，我会准时收听你的撞击球专题节目。

1584
01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:14.480
You're going to be there, lady.
你到时候也会在场的，女士。

1585
01:14:14.660 --> 01:14:15.500
Oh, I'll be there.
噢，我肯定会在。

1586
01:14:17.300 --> 01:14:17.740
Okay.
好的。

1587
01:14:18.360 --> 01:14:19.180
Look for it.
敬请期待。

1588
01:14:19.320 --> 01:14:20.100
This winter.
就在今年冬天。

1589
01:14:20.300 --> 01:14:20.620
Yeah.
没错。

1590
01:14:20.820 --> 01:14:22.460
Special episode, bonus episode.
特别节目，番外篇。

1591
01:14:22.460 --> 01:14:24.780
Office Ladies, semicolon, clacky balls.
《办公室女士》，分号，撞击球。

1592
01:14:25.780 --> 01:14:29.580
Well, Michael is going to try to convince the sales team that things are going to get better.
迈克尔打算说服销售团队，情况会好转的。

1593
01:14:29.780 --> 01:14:30.380
They are.
确实会好转。

1594
01:14:30.600 --> 01:14:33.080
That Danny being there will no longer be a threat.
丹尼在那里将不再是个威胁。

1595
01:14:33.080 --> 01:14:34.300
He'll now be an asset.
他现在会成为一个助力。

1596
01:14:34.800 --> 01:14:40.520
Right after this, Danny is going to tell Jim that he and Pam went on a few dates way back,
就在这之后，丹尼会告诉吉姆，他和帕姆很久以前约会过几次，

1597
01:14:40.620 --> 01:14:41.760
but that Pam wasn't into him.
但帕姆对他没意思。

1598
01:14:41.980 --> 01:14:42.760
Didn't call him back.
没回他的电话。

1599
01:14:43.740 --> 01:14:44.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1600
01:14:44.720 --> 01:14:45.020
Uh-oh.
噢哦。

1601
01:14:45.260 --> 01:14:46.580
Jim's like, she told me.
吉姆说，她告诉了我。

1602
01:14:47.220 --> 01:14:47.920
I know.
我知道。

1603
01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:52.000
But then Dwight overhears this and has such a strong reaction.
但德怀特听到了，反应非常强烈。

1604
01:14:52.000 --> 01:14:54.480
He's like, let me handle this, Jim.
他说，吉姆，让我来处理。

1605
01:14:55.020 --> 01:14:56.520
Drop the act, Cordray, okay?
别装了，科德雷，好吗？

1606
01:14:56.520 --> 01:15:02.260
We all know that you probably thought that Pam was just too meh or thin without being toned.
我们都知道你可能觉得帕姆太平庸，或者瘦得没线条。

1607
01:15:02.440 --> 01:15:03.540
But I want to tell you something.
但我得告诉你一件事。

1608
01:15:03.700 --> 01:15:08.260
She is one of the plain, hardy women of Scranton that make this city great.
她是斯克兰顿那些朴实坚韧的女性之一，正是她们让这座城市变得伟大。

1609
01:15:08.260 --> 01:15:10.400
And so what if she doesn't wear makeup?
就算她不化妆又怎样？

1610
01:15:11.280 --> 01:15:19.600
Lady, when we did the table read and I heard the line, thin without being toned, I laughed so hard.
女士，当我们读剧本时，听到那句“瘦得没线条”，我笑得不行。

1611
01:15:19.800 --> 01:15:23.880
I was like, that is such an accurate description of my physique.
我当时就想，这简直是对我身材的精准描述。

1612
01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:27.240
I was like, they nailed it.
我觉得他们说得太对了。

1613
01:15:27.340 --> 01:15:28.820
And it was so funny to me.
这对我来说太搞笑了。

1614
01:15:28.980 --> 01:15:32.220
I loved when Pam mouths to the camera, I wear makeup.
我特别喜欢帕姆对着镜头做口型说“我化妆了”的那一段。

1615
01:15:33.180 --> 01:15:35.520
Also, I love he describes her as meh.
而且，我喜欢他用“平庸”来形容她。

1616
01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:36.040
Meh.
平庸。

1617
01:15:36.480 --> 01:15:37.600
That was very funny.
那真的太好笑了。

1618
01:15:37.820 --> 01:15:38.640
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1619
01:15:39.040 --> 01:15:44.300
Dwight is also going to accuse Danny of being a thief, but then finds out it's five o'clock and shakes his hand.
德怀特还要指控丹尼是小偷，但后来发现到五点了，又跟他握手言和。

1620
01:15:44.420 --> 01:15:45.940
No, he's not going to take that home with him.
不，他不会把那种情绪带回家的。

1621
01:15:46.040 --> 01:15:47.300
He's not going to take that energy home.
他不会把那种负能量带回家。

1622
01:15:47.980 --> 01:15:54.180
Well, even though Andy, Daryl, and Kevin were all upstairs to meet Danny Cordray,
虽然安迪、达里尔和凯文都在楼上见丹尼·科德雷，

1623
01:15:54.320 --> 01:15:56.900
they're also simultaneously down in the warehouse.
但他们同时也出现在仓库里。

1624
01:15:57.160 --> 01:15:58.840
I don't know if you noticed this editing.
不知道你有没有注意到这个剪辑。

1625
01:15:58.940 --> 01:16:01.200
They managed to be in two places at once.
他们竟然能同时出现在两个地方。

1626
01:16:01.260 --> 01:16:01.940
They're magic.
他们有魔法。

1627
01:16:01.940 --> 01:16:08.140
And they're down there, and first, Andy tries to write a song from the heart.
他们在那儿，起初，安迪试着写一首走心的歌。

1628
01:16:08.380 --> 01:16:08.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1629
01:16:09.300 --> 01:16:10.380
It's okay.
还行。

1630
01:16:10.720 --> 01:16:11.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1631
01:16:11.380 --> 01:16:12.860
But they've run out of time.
但他们的时间不够了。

1632
01:16:13.440 --> 01:16:14.460
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1633
01:16:14.800 --> 01:16:18.500
Daryl is going to stay, and he's going to jam for free.
达里尔决定留下来，免费陪他们即兴演奏。

1634
01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:19.220
Yeah.
没错。

1635
01:16:19.720 --> 01:16:20.860
Andy's so happy.
安迪太开心了。

1636
01:16:21.480 --> 01:16:25.140
And as a result, they are going to write a fabulous song.
结果，他们写出了一首绝妙的歌。

1637
01:16:25.380 --> 01:16:29.540
It's titled, Croak, Croak, Croak, Bullfrog and Love.
歌名是《呱，呱，呱，牛蛙与爱》。

1638
01:16:29.540 --> 01:16:32.040
We had a fan question from Nicole S.
我们收到一个来自华盛顿州西雅图的粉丝妮可·S的提问，

1639
01:16:32.080 --> 01:16:35.280
in Seattle, Washington, who wanted to know who wrote Bullfrog
她想知道是谁写了《牛蛙

1640
01:16:35.280 --> 01:16:37.060
and Love, because it's really great.
与爱》，因为这首歌真的很棒。

1641
01:16:37.700 --> 01:16:42.400
Well, this one was lyrics by Mindy Kaling and music by Eve Nelson.
嗯，这首歌的歌词是敏迪·卡灵写的，曲子是伊芙·尼尔森写的。

1642
01:16:43.180 --> 01:16:44.560
It is very good.
真的非常好听。

1643
01:16:44.700 --> 01:16:45.280
Very catchy.
非常洗脑。

1644
01:16:45.680 --> 01:16:47.240
Well, Nicole, we agree with you.
妮可，我们和你意见一致。

1645
01:16:47.420 --> 01:16:48.440
It's pretty awesome.
这首歌真的很赞。

1646
01:16:48.460 --> 01:16:50.320
And we all think you need to hear it.
我们都觉得你应该听听看。

1647
01:16:50.320 --> 01:16:54.630
Stars in her eyes, tongue full of flies.
眼中闪烁星光，舌尖满是苍蝇。

1648
01:16:54.650 --> 01:16:57.010
Would you like to share my past?
你愿意分享我的过去吗？

1649
01:16:57.670 --> 01:17:00.530
Croak, croak, croak, Bullfrog and Love.
呱，呱，呱，牛蛙与爱。

1650
01:17:02.190 --> 01:17:04.990
A croak, croak, croak, Bullfrog and Love.
呱，呱，呱，牛蛙与爱。

1651
01:17:05.110 --> 01:17:07.670
And I gave her the croak that meant I love you.
我用那声蛙鸣告诉她我爱你。

1652
01:17:08.090 --> 01:17:10.030
I'll be your croak, monsieur.
我愿做你的蛙鸣，先生。

1653
01:17:10.990 --> 01:17:13.830
I'll be your croak.
我愿做你的蛙鸣。

1654
01:17:13.830 --> 01:17:17.990
My mind said that Bullfrog's a dog, but I'm here to tell you that I am a frog.
我的理智告诉我牛蛙是狗，但我现在要告诉你，我是一只青蛙。

1655
01:17:18.230 --> 01:17:20.710
Come and sit on my log, you little polly walk.
来吧，坐在我的圆木上，你这只小蝌蚪。

1656
01:17:21.130 --> 01:17:23.370
I find you absolutely riveting.
我觉得你真是太迷人了。

1657
01:17:23.970 --> 01:17:26.190
Croak, croak, croak, Bullfrog and Love.
呱，呱，呱，牛蛙与爱。

1658
